<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ochlockonee River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ochlockonee River rises in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and flows about 330 kilometres south through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> Panhandle to Ochlockonee Bay on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>. Together with the Aucilla to the east, it bounded the heartland of the Apalachee people. It passes west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tallahassee">Tallahassee</a> and feeds the reservoir of Lake Talquin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ochlockonee-river.jpg" alt="Ochlockonee River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tim Ross · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:06-09_OchlockAtOldBnbrdgRd.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
